From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:49:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: gts3lwifi: Deep sleep (MPM, L2 and system
 power collapse)

The two deepest idle states the stock kernel uses, L2 power collapse
(0x01000044) and system power collapse (0x02003444), which Samsung's
TrustZone grants, as the last cluster and system domain-idle-states, and
the RPM's MPM, which upstream does not describe for msm8996: the driver
programs the vMPM wake-up timer and routes the PMIC's wake-ups (pin 87,
the power key and the RTC alarm), so the RPM can turn XO off, lower the
rails (vmin) and wake the system again. The CPU state stays mode 4
(TrustZone keeps the context).

Needs CONFIG_QCOM_MPM: the PMIC's interrupts go through the MPM. The LTE
model includes this DTS; its running modem keeps the system out of vmin.

On an SM-T820, two back-to-back 60 s suspends spent 60.7 s and 61.4 s in
vmin (with Wi-Fi's PCIe controller disabled); the power key and the RTC
alarm wake it.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts    | 78 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 78 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts
index ef1af0b3b..347ccacfc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts
@@ -2304,3 +2304,81 @@ channel@77 {
 &{/firmware/scm} {
 	memory-region = <&qseecom_mem>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Deep sleep: L2 power collapse and system power collapse as the
+ * deepest cluster and system idle states, the way stock's lpm-levels
+ * compose them (CPU mode 0 bit, cluster mode 4, system 0x34, affinity 24;
+ * reset bit 30 only from the CPU level, which stock never sets). The TZ
+ * grants 0x01000044 / 0x02003444 (the bit-30 forms are NOT_SUPPORTED).
+ * Plus the MPM: in system power collapse the CPUs' arch timers stop and
+ * wake-up interrupts other than the memory-mapped timer reach the CPUs only
+ * through the RPM's MPM, which mainline does not describe for msm8996. The
+ * driver (irqchip/qcom-mpm) programs the vMPM wake-up timer and routes the
+ * PMIC's wakes (pin 87) so the RPM can wake the AP from vmin.
+ */
+/ {
+	domain-idle-states {
+		cluster_pc: cluster-pc {
+			compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+			arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x01000044>;
+			entry-latency-us = <400>;
+			exit-latency-us = <700>;
+			min-residency-us = <5000>;
+		};
+
+		system_pc: system-pc {
+			compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+			arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x02003444>;
+			entry-latency-us = <4000>;
+			exit-latency-us = <11000>;
+			min-residency-us = <50000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&cluster0_pd {
+	domain-idle-states = <&cluster_gdhs>, <&cluster_pc>;
+};
+
+&cluster1_pd {
+	domain-idle-states = <&cluster_gdhs>, <&cluster_pc>;
+};
+
+&system_pd {
+	domain-idle-states = <&system_ret>, <&system_pc>;
+	power-domains = <&mpm>;
+};
+
+&rpm_msg_ram {
+	compatible = "qcom,rpm-msg-ram", "mmio-sram";
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <1>;
+	ranges = <0 0x00068000 0x6000>;
+
+	apss_mpm: sram@1b8 {
+		reg = <0x1b8 0x48>;
+	};
+};
+
+&rpm {
+	mpm: interrupt-controller {
+		compatible = "qcom,mpm";
+		qcom,rpm-msg-ram = <&apss_mpm>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 171 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		mboxes = <&apcs_glb 1>;
+		interrupt-controller;
+		#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
+		qcom,mpm-pin-count = <96>;
+		qcom,mpm-pin-map = <2 184>,
+				   <52 180>,
+				   <87 326>;	/* SPMI PMIC arbiter */
+	};
+};
+
+&spmi_bus {
+	/delete-property/ interrupts;
+	interrupts-extended = <&mpm 87 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+};
